<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>CFBundleName</key>
    <string>Tasks_agent_loop</string>
    <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
    <string>Tasks_agent_loop</string>
    <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
    <string>dev.cplus.tasksagentloop</string>
    <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
    <string>1.0</string>
    <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
    <string>1</string>
    <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
    <string>APPL</string>
    <key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. macOS refuses a permission to an app
         that has not said what it wants it FOR, and the refusal is
         not a `Denied` you can handle: `permissions::request` kills
         the process, asynchronously, after the call has already
         returned. The string is shown to the person in the dialog,
         so write it for them and not for the compiler.

         Uncomment what this app actually asks for. Leaving one in
         that the app never requests is harmless; leaving one OUT
         that it does request is fatal at runtime. -->

